		{
			dependencies: ["610FD2C783821A4E"]
			description: [
				"Abyss Catalysis adds two new items and over 20 new recipes for you to discover and create."
				""
				"To begin, you must first forge the Abyssal Chamber through Mechanical Crafting."
				""
				"You will also need to construct a Mechanical Shrieker to activate the chamber’s reactions."
				""
				"With this technology, you can imbue the power of items such as Ender Pearls and Nether Stars to transmutate materials into something entirely new. "
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Some recipes require heat to function. Be sure to place a Blaze Burner beneath the chamber for those that demand it."
				""
				"The setup pictured below demonstrates a basic configuration used to create End Stone. You know it is working properly when you see the blue particle effect emitting from the Mechanical Shrieker."
				""
				"{image:ftb:textures/abyss_catalysis_end_stone.png width:220 height:220 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Pay close attention to the positioning of ingredients in each recipe:"
				""
				"- The top-left item goes into the inverted basin on top."
				"- The bottom-left item goes into the upright basin below."
				"- The right-side item is placed into the center of the chamber."
				""
				"Some recipes feature a chance ingredient, which is an item that is only consumed a certain percentage of the time."
				""
				"For example, in the Dragon Head recipe, the Nether Star in the right slot has only a 5% chance to be used per operation."
				""
				"{image:ftb:textures/abyss_catalysis_chance_ingredient.png width:198 height:135 align:center}"
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
